    <section class="word-day" aria-labelledby="word-day">
      <h2 id="word-day">Word of the day</h2>
      <p class="word-greek">ruth</p>
      <p>
        Butler’s Apollo says Achilles “knows neither right nor ruth.” Ruth is
        pity. It is the old English word for the compassion this lesson adds.
        Find “ruth” in the speech of Apollo, then find Priam kissing the hands.
        The Greek word is not printed in this translation. The act is.
      </p>
    </section>

